#: includes/abilities/class-notification-abilities.php:756
msgid "Creates a new notification from one of the starter templates and always saves it as a draft, so nothing fires until a human (or notification-master/set-notification-status with status publish) enables it. Template ids come from notification-master/list-starter-templates and look like tpl_post-published. Each template ships five connections: email to administrators and web push to every subscriber (both enabled), plus disabled Discord, webhook and Instagram shells whose URLs and credentials still have to be filled in wp-admin. Templates exist only for triggers registered on this site; there are no WooCommerce templates in either tier, so an unknown id answers 400 ntfm_invalid_template with the allowed ids. The reply lists the new id and the next action that would enable it. Nothing is sent by this call."
